# Two `=` in one projection (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
T | project a = b = c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..22
  PIPELINE@0..21
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "T"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    PROJECT_OP@4..21
      IDENT@4..11 "project"
      WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
      NAMED_EXPR@12..21
        NAME@12..13
          IDENT@12..13 "a"
        WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
        EQ@14..15 "="
        WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
        BIN_EXPR@16..21
          NAME_REF@16..17
            IDENT@16..17 "b"
          WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
          EQ@18..19 "="
          WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
          NAME_REF@20..21
            IDENT@20..21 "c"
  WHITESPACE@21..22 "\n"

error[DS0110]: `=` is assignment, not comparison
  --> query:1:19
  |
1 | T | project a = b = c
  |                   ^ assignment is not allowed here
  |
  = help: use `==` to compare values: `b == c`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    T | project a = b == c
which parses without errors
